  "title": "Let’s talk about the doomsday glacier 🧊  Thwaites Glacier has been co...",
  "description": "Let’s talk about the doomsday glacier 🧊  Thwaites Glacier has been coined the “doomsday glacier” due to its potential to cause an irreversible feedback loop where other glaciers melt if it collapses. Although substantial melt is inevitable, it’s important to know that a collapse isn’t at this time. The headlines you might have seen recently regarding the “doomsday glacier” are discussing one study, and based on my conversations with colleagues that study is not as conclusive as the media made it out to be. There is still much to learn about Thwaites and its impact on other ice formations in Antarctica - which is why scientists are actively conducting research on it. While it is true that climate change has already caused significant changes to our polar regions, that doesn’t mean it’s too late to mitigate future impacts or adapt to the ones we’re already experiencing. We can protect ice formations from future melt if we quickly reduce emissions on a global scale, and we can also protect coastal communities from the impacts of what’s already melted. This won’t be easy, but it’s necessary. So don’t give up. Keep fighting for climate action and justice. #DoomsdayGlacier #ThwaitesGlacier #Thwaites #Antarctica #ClimateChange #ClimateCrisis",
